# Migration plan (Lab → product)

The Design Lab is frozen as the visual reference. Migrate in this order — do not
skip lots; do not start Accueil before Shell and Match.

## Lot 0 — Final arbitrations ✅

- Angle: **12°**
- Width: fluid 100% with lateral gutters (no centered max-width column)
- Match Hero, numeric roles, icon rules, surface hierarchy — validated in Lab V2

## Lot 1 — Foundations ✅

Tokens (brand-deep/bright, live), typography (numeric roles), brand CSS,
`PlayUpWordmark`, `TrendIcon`, `LiveStatus`, `metaIcons`, numbers + live
foundations. Design Lab consumes DS (no parallel `--dlab-*` tokens).

## Lot 2 — Shell ✅

Rail + header foundations (`foundations/shell.css`), product shell aligned
(wordmark 22px + `PlayUpWordmark`, skewed nav bar, competition header grammar).
Design Lab consumes `ds-shell-*`.

## Lot 3 — Match ✅

Match Hero, MatchRow, timeline, panel grammar in `foundations/match.css` +
`foundations/panels.css`. Product: `MatchPage` (hero + grid 1.45/1), `MatchHubPage`
(rows), goals timeline. Design Lab consumes DS match components.

## Lot 4 — Cockpit ✅

Cockpit grammar in `foundations/cockpit.css` — situation num, cycle, next action,
attention rows (D9), mini-table, podium. Components: `CockpitSituation`,
`CockpitNextAction`, `AttentionGroup`/`AttentionRow`, `CycleLine`, `CockpitPodium`.
Product: `CompetitionCockpitPage` (next action, attention, podium, DS `PanelHead`).
Design Lab consumes DS cockpit components.

## Lot 5 — Classements / Calendrier

Numeric grammar at full intensity (zones, trends, matchdays).

## Lot 6 — Accueil

Brand entry point — after the operational grammar is proven.

## Lot 7 — Legacy purge

Anything that does not match the Design Lab is suspect. Remove `index.css` legacy
palette, pills, ghost tokens, duplicated components.

## Rule during migration

Each lot must pass the acceptance test: **could this have been designed in the Lab?**
If not, extend the Lab first (gap only — no new artistic direction).
